WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:03.136
-Our first guest tonight hosts
"Deadline: White House" weekdays

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:05.338
from 4:00 to 6:00 p.m. on MSNBC.

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:07.139
Please welcome back to the show
Nicolle Wallace.

00:00:07.139 --> 00:00:09.375
Nicolle, how are you?

00:00:09.375 --> 00:00:10.676
-I'm good.

00:00:10.676 --> 00:00:13.413
I have to say, I was on TV
for most of it

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:16.616
and hadn't processed it
until I heard your summation,

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:19.619
and I couldn't have said it
better myself.

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:21.253
I mean, that is
exactly where we are.

00:00:21.253 --> 00:00:23.890
That's exactly
what happened today.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:27.459
-I want to thank you
for the fact that you were on TV

00:00:27.459 --> 00:00:30.596
very late last night,
covering the Georgia runoffs,

00:00:30.596 --> 00:00:33.366
and then, of course, you were
kept on camera all day today,

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:34.634
as you mentioned.

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:38.104
So thank you so much
for finding time for us as well.

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:40.940
Are you exhausted?

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.108
-No. I mean, look,

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:46.512
there are people
who have so much more at risk.

00:00:46.512 --> 00:00:50.350
And I'm just ruminating on
what you said about

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:52.618
what has to happen to the people

00:00:52.618 --> 00:00:55.488
who supported
today's insurrection

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:58.324
in Congress
and the sedition caucus

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:01.594
that were carrying out
a fake thing.

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:05.397
There is no legislative vehicle
for overthrowing

00:01:05.397 --> 00:01:08.467
the results of an election
that was fair,

00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:11.003
that was verified,
that was counted and recounted,

00:01:11.003 --> 00:01:14.974
that was litigated in 60 court
cases across the country

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:17.810
from coast to coast by judges
from both political parties.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:21.013
So the only thing I would add to
this group of people,

00:01:21.013 --> 00:01:22.748
starting with Donald Trump

00:01:22.748 --> 00:01:25.317
but also the 12 Republican
Senators

00:01:25.317 --> 00:01:27.020
and more than 100 House members

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.155
and all of the supporters of
Donald Trump's

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:30.623
who were at the Capitol today,

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:32.892
endangering the lives of
everybody inside --

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:37.163
staffers, members of Congress,
senators, the police officers --

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:38.931
we have to make sure that people

00:01:38.931 --> 00:01:42.568
who are on the other side of
democracy get voted out as well.

00:01:42.568 --> 00:01:44.103
I mean, Donald Trump
should be removed

00:01:44.103 --> 00:01:46.472
because he is,
right now at this hour,

00:01:46.472 --> 00:01:48.441
a national security threat.

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:50.143
And I worked in a White House

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:52.512
where we dealt with
national security threats

00:01:52.512 --> 00:01:54.079
in a very different way

00:01:54.079 --> 00:01:55.481
than they're being dealt with
right now.

00:01:55.481 --> 00:01:56.882
But that's what Donald Trump is.

00:01:56.882 --> 00:01:58.150
He's a clear and present danger

00:01:58.150 --> 00:02:00.519
to the country
he ostensibly leads.

00:02:00.519 --> 00:02:02.655
But even that is unclear
at this hour.

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:05.591
It was reported that Mike Pence
was the one that authorized

00:02:05.591 --> 00:02:09.261
the National Guard coming in
to aid Capitol police.

00:02:09.261 --> 00:02:11.597
-You mentioned your time
in the White House,

00:02:11.597 --> 00:02:15.868
and you were obviously working
in the White House during 9/11.

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:18.938
And you've mentioned today
to some of your guests

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:21.274
that you had a flashback to that

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:24.077
because it must have been
terrifying for those

00:02:24.077 --> 00:02:26.745
that were in both chambers
when this was going down.

00:02:26.745 --> 00:02:31.417
-Yeah. Well, Congresswoman
Linda Sanchez came on the air

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:35.321
and said that last night she
called her husband in California

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:37.623
and told him where he could find
her will.

00:02:37.623 --> 00:02:41.127
So last night Congresswoman
Linda Sanchez thought

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:43.862
it was possible that today
she would die at work.

00:02:43.862 --> 00:02:45.765
She works in the Capitol.

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:49.735
So it is inexplicable to me
if she thought yesterday

00:02:49.735 --> 00:02:54.707
enough concern that she told
her husband where her will was,

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:56.542
and she has an 11-year-old son,

00:02:56.542 --> 00:02:58.678
she got very emotional
telling me this story,

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:00.913
why didn't the Capitol police

00:03:00.913 --> 00:03:03.816
have a better plan
than they had?

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:06.552
I mean, it didn't appear that
the protesters, the rioters,

00:03:06.552 --> 00:03:08.621
met any resistance at all.

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:13.192
And to me where
this was similar to 9/11

00:03:13.192 --> 00:03:15.094
was that both chambers
were evacuated.

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:18.464
Members went to
undisclosed locations

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:19.632
and they sheltered in place.

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:21.700
What was different
was the response.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.937
I mean, after 9/11, many of
the things that this country did

00:03:24.937 --> 00:03:28.341
in the name of making sure that
terrorists never flew airplanes

00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:30.342
into the World Trade Center
or the Pentagon

00:03:30.342 --> 00:03:35.147
or crashed in Pennsylvania
will be polarizing decisions.

00:03:35.147 --> 00:03:36.649
But everything changed.

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:39.819
Today the Republicans went back
to the floor of the Senate

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:42.522
and six Senators still sought

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:44.757
to overturn the results
of the election,

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:47.626
still sought to delegitimize
Joe Biden's win.

00:03:47.626 --> 00:03:50.062
So what's disturbing to me

00:03:50.062 --> 00:03:53.132
is more the ways that it was
different from 9/11,

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:56.835
that we didn't wake up from
this sort of drunken stupor

00:03:56.835 --> 00:03:59.438
of disinformation
and lies and smears

00:03:59.438 --> 00:04:01.507
that endanger, at this point,
all of us.

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:05.678
-Yeah. There was a moment that I
think was also very clear-eyed

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:07.747
where, you know, Mitt Romney
took the floor

00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:11.517
and basically said we have to
tell these people the truth

00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:15.254
because when we lie to them,
they're very upset by reality.

00:04:15.254 --> 00:04:20.693
And yet as you mentioned, people
came back into the chamber

00:04:20.693 --> 00:04:22.895
and, you know,
ostensibly this is about

00:04:22.895 --> 00:04:24.096
"Hey, we want evidence.

00:04:24.096 --> 00:04:26.065
We can't move forward
unless there's evidence."

00:04:26.065 --> 00:04:29.568
And yet if you listen to some
members of the House tonight,

00:04:29.568 --> 00:04:33.940
if you watch
right-wing cable news,

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:36.876
the speed at which they're
saying this was actually Antifa,

00:04:36.876 --> 00:04:41.847
now, obviously, that is a claim
that cannot this soon after what

00:04:41.847 --> 00:04:44.116
we just saw be made
with any evidence.

00:04:44.116 --> 00:04:46.285
And so that I think is
the most terrifying thing,

00:04:46.285 --> 00:04:50.423
is how quickly, as you point
out, it went back to normal.

00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:53.792
-And it suggests that
we're just in the --

00:04:53.792 --> 00:04:55.327
you know, we're in grooves now.

00:04:55.327 --> 00:04:58.430
And I think --
you know, I thought this a lot

00:04:58.430 --> 00:05:02.968
as we floundered and failed to
contain and protect one another

00:05:02.968 --> 00:05:06.272
from COVID, that if Donald Trump
were the president

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:08.441
and the disinformation
were in place,

00:05:08.441 --> 00:05:11.777
you could see people refusing
to abide by TSA requirements

00:05:11.777 --> 00:05:13.245
and say, "I'm not taking off
my shoes

00:05:13.245 --> 00:05:15.247
or throwing away
my Fiji water bottle.

00:05:15.247 --> 00:05:16.683
It cost me $4."

00:05:16.683 --> 00:05:21.621
We are not the same country that
we were on September 11, 2001.

00:05:21.621 --> 00:05:24.824
We are not represented by
the same kinds of leaders.

00:05:24.824 --> 00:05:28.127
There is -- Clearly after today
there is nothing

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:32.231
that jolts them out of their --
and it's not partisanship.

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:34.199
This isn't in the name
of the Republican Party.

00:05:34.199 --> 00:05:37.169
This is in the name of
a cult leader, Donald Trump.

00:05:37.169 --> 00:05:40.472
-You know, we're often told
that, you know,

00:05:40.472 --> 00:05:43.276
senators like Josh Hawley,
like Ted Cruz,

00:05:43.276 --> 00:05:45.377
these are brilliant lawyers.

00:05:45.377 --> 00:05:46.779
You know,
Donald Trump's one thing,

00:05:46.779 --> 00:05:48.914
but these are intelligent men.

00:05:48.914 --> 00:05:50.516
These are serious men.

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:55.354
And yet when you watch
what they did today,

00:05:55.354 --> 00:05:57.255
were you surprised

00:05:57.255 --> 00:06:02.561
or is this in line with
their behavior in the Trump era?

00:06:02.561 --> 00:06:07.299
-You know, I thought on election
day that Trump was like

00:06:07.299 --> 00:06:11.904
a popped balloon, that he was no
longer the most newsworthy part

00:06:11.904 --> 00:06:14.673
of this really terrible moment
in our politics.

00:06:14.673 --> 00:06:18.844
And I instantly started covering
much more aggressively

00:06:18.844 --> 00:06:22.948
the Republican enablers because
I thought if, after the election

00:06:22.948 --> 00:06:26.552
was lost by Donald Trump,
if all the Republicans,

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:29.821
if Mitch McConnell and Kevin
McCarthy and all the Republicans

00:06:29.821 --> 00:06:33.525
came out and said,
"Hey, we voted for you, Donald,"

00:06:33.525 --> 00:06:35.594
because we know he's a big baby,
they had to make clear

00:06:35.594 --> 00:06:37.462
that they were there for him,
"but the country went

00:06:37.462 --> 00:06:39.865
a different direction,
better luck next time,"

00:06:39.865 --> 00:06:41.266
that none of this
would have happened.

00:06:41.266 --> 00:06:43.336
And I believe that about today.

00:06:43.336 --> 00:06:46.272
So with that stipulated,
I actually think

00:06:46.272 --> 00:06:49.408
the more egregious offenders
to our democracy,

00:06:49.408 --> 00:06:52.878
the people putting all of us in
danger and capable of doing so

00:06:52.878 --> 00:06:56.315
after January 20th are
the Josh Hawleys of the world.

00:06:56.315 --> 00:07:00.185
And if one more person says on
our air how well-educated he is,

00:07:00.185 --> 00:07:02.822
he may be well-educated
but he's clearly not smart.

00:07:02.822 --> 00:07:06.125
Or if he's smart he doesn't care
about the country he lives in

00:07:06.125 --> 00:07:08.093
or the fact that
it's a democracy.

00:07:08.093 --> 00:07:10.663
-I think it's really important
to stress that

00:07:10.663 --> 00:07:12.998
our nation's best universities

00:07:12.998 --> 00:07:14.933
are filled with
some real dummies.

00:07:14.933 --> 00:07:16.802
And that has always
been the way.

00:07:16.802 --> 00:07:19.172
-And conversely
our public universities

00:07:19.172 --> 00:07:21.239
turn out some good folks.
-Yes, absolutely.

00:07:21.239 --> 00:07:23.909
It's a mistake to think
what's on the diploma

00:07:23.909 --> 00:07:28.347
speaks certainly to
the character of a person.

00:07:28.347 --> 00:07:31.617
You know, I feel as though
people like myself maybe

00:07:31.617 --> 00:07:36.354
have been framed as being
overreactive or hysterical

00:07:36.354 --> 00:07:43.128
when we point out, you know,
how awful it is to say,

00:07:43.128 --> 00:07:44.830
after Charlottesville, you know,
there are good people

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:47.132
on both sides or to say,
during a debate, you know,

00:07:47.132 --> 00:07:52.471
Proud Boys, you know,
"Stand back but stand by"

00:07:52.471 --> 00:07:55.174
or, you know,
to use the word "coup."

00:07:55.174 --> 00:07:58.043
This always seemed like
these were the cards

00:07:58.043 --> 00:07:59.645
that Donald Trump
was showing us.

00:07:59.645 --> 00:08:03.415
And it always seemed
as though -- and you hoped,

00:08:03.415 --> 00:08:05.518
obviously, you were wrong,
but it did seem like

00:08:05.518 --> 00:08:07.953
it was heading toward
something like this.

00:08:07.953 --> 00:08:10.956
-Look, I think the lookback
on all of us

00:08:10.956 --> 00:08:13.092
will be that
we weren't harsh enough.

00:08:13.092 --> 00:08:16.128
Why did it take us --
It took us a couple years.

00:08:16.128 --> 00:08:17.763
And I was one of
the first to stop

00:08:17.763 --> 00:08:20.566
airing Sarah Huckabee Sanders,
but I wasn't fast enough.

00:08:20.566 --> 00:08:23.369
I always called Donald Trump
a liar and a racist

00:08:23.369 --> 00:08:25.504
and a misogynist,
but I didn't do it early enough.

00:08:25.504 --> 00:08:28.407
I wish I'd done it
before the election in 2016.

00:08:28.407 --> 00:08:32.945
And so I think part of what the
mob mentality on the Trump side

00:08:32.945 --> 00:08:35.981
has done is
successfully bully people.

00:08:35.981 --> 00:08:38.083
They call it
Trump derangement syndrome.

00:08:38.083 --> 00:08:40.119
"Oh, you don't understand
the other half of the country."

00:08:40.119 --> 00:08:42.287
It's not about understanding
the other half of the country.

00:08:42.287 --> 00:08:46.859
I think that you and a lot of
people that had worked in

00:08:46.859 --> 00:08:48.393
government before watched him,

00:08:48.393 --> 00:08:53.399
and he wasn't doing anything
in the spirit of the state.

00:08:53.399 --> 00:08:57.069
He never saw the country
as attached to him

00:08:57.069 --> 00:08:58.838
or as something
he was responsible for.

00:08:58.838 --> 00:09:01.306
He always saw it
as a possession of his.

00:09:01.306 --> 00:09:05.378
Like, you know, he talks
about women as objects.

00:09:05.378 --> 00:09:07.980
He talks about --
He talks about people

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:11.250
and the United States government
and the United States military

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:14.219
and his hotels the very same way
because to him

00:09:14.219 --> 00:09:17.022
they are all objects
that he possesses and controls.

00:09:17.022 --> 00:09:20.626
And so I think that the lookback
will be that we were not

00:09:20.626 --> 00:09:24.396
hard enough on him, we were not
aggressive enough as journalists

00:09:24.396 --> 00:09:27.265
in covering him and we did not
draw people's attention

00:09:27.265 --> 00:09:32.037
to the grave threat that we now
face from him right now today

00:09:32.037 --> 00:09:34.440
in his remaining days
as our country's only president.

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:36.174
We only have one at a time.

00:09:36.174 --> 00:09:40.779
And last time I checked my phone
unfortunately he's still it.

00:09:40.779 --> 00:09:43.382
-We're going to be right back
after this

00:09:43.382 --> 00:09:44.717
with more from Nicolle Wallace.

